<title>USA: AMERICAN STANDARD FILES $1 BLN DEBT SHELF.</title>
<headline>AMERICAN STANDARD FILES $1 BLN DEBT SHELF.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Standard Cos Inc filed with  the Securities and Exchange Commission on Friday to register a shelf  offering of up to $1 billion in debt securities.</p>
<p>No underwriters were named in the shelf offering.</p>
<p>The proceeds of the sale will be used for general corporate purposes,  which may include reducing outstanding debt, stock repurchases and  capital expenditures.</p>
</text>
